<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Negüder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Nigudar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Negüder was a Mongol commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> who led Jochid troops sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> with Hülegü's expedition in the 1250s. When war broke out between the Golden Horde and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> in 1262, his men, cut off in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, became an independent force, the Negüderis, raiding Khurasan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. They later merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaraunas">Qara'unas</a> of the Chagatai and Timurid era.</p></div>
